<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolfo López Mateos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolfo López Mateos was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> from 1958 to 1964 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/institutional-revolutionary-party">Institutional Revolutionary Party</a>. His government nationalised the electricity industry in 1960, expanded land distribution, social security and free school textbooks, and crushed the railway workers' strike of 1959. In foreign affairs he kept relations with revolutionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and began the diplomacy that led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tlatelolco">Treaty of Tlatelolco</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adolfo-lopez-mateos.jpg" alt="Adolfo López Mateos" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harry Pot for Anefo ]] · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolfo_L%C3%B3pez_Mateos_(1963)_(cropped)(c).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
